This product depends on / uses:
================================================================================

Runtime dependencies
--------------------

- uni-db (Apache-2.0)
  The embedded multi-model graph engine that uniko is built on. Provides
  graph storage, OpenCypher querying, Locy logic programming, and
  vector/hybrid search. https://crates.io/crates/uni-db

- uni-xervo (license: see upstream)
  Model runtime used to register and invoke local ONNX models (embeddings,
  NLP cascade, and cross-encoder reranker) and to route remote providers.
  https://crates.io/crates/uni-xervo

- ONNX Runtime, via the `ort` crate (ONNX Runtime: MIT; `ort` crate: see upstream)
  Inference engine used to execute the local ONNX embedding, NLP, and
  reranker models at write-time and during recall.

- tree-sitter (MIT) and language grammars tree-sitter-python,
  tree-sitter-rust, tree-sitter-javascript, tree-sitter-typescript
  (license: see upstream)
  Incremental parsers used for code-aware chunking and extraction.

Other notable third-party runtime crates (each under its own license;
see upstream for exact terms) include: serde / serde_json / serde_yaml,
chrono, uuid, thiserror, anyhow, async-trait, rand, tokio / tokio-util /
futures, metrics / metrics-exporter-prometheus, tracing /
tracing-subscriber, tiktoken-rs, ndarray, tokenizers, rust-stemmers,
regex, lru, sha2, hex, and object_store. A complete, authoritative
dependency-and-license inventory is enforced in CI via cargo-deny.

Default models
--------------

uniko ships with no model weights. The following models are referenced as
defaults and are downloaded from their upstream sources (e.g. the Hugging
Face Hub) at runtime. Each model is governed by its own upstream license
and terms of use; consult the upstream model card before redistribution
or production use.

- BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 (license: see upstream)
  Default text embedding model (384-dimensional). Used to produce vector
  embeddings for hybrid search.

- dragonscale-ai/kniv-deberta-nlp-base-en-xsmall (license: see upstream)
  Default NLP cascade model (INT8 ONNX, artifact `onnx/cascade-int8.onnx`).
  Used at write-time for local NER, observation, and related NLP
  extraction — no LLM in the recall hot path.

- cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2 (license: see upstream)
  Default cross-encoder reranker. Used to re-score top hybrid-search
  candidates during recall.

